(text "J190 is the single AUX/SOLAR physical input; USB-C PD negotiation remains only on sheet 5." (at 379.73 20.32 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid f07a0945-41be-575b-b4f0-5728c476a94b))
(text "TPS26630 accepts 7-22V nominal; 0.1% ladder targets 5.53V/22.99V rising UV/OV and a 3A limit." (at 379.73 25.4 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid 29b017f8-f508-5df6-a902-2df8dc68b4d1))
(text "U15/U16 accepts fixed 5/9/15/20V PD contracts and AUX across 7-22V; priority remains PD1 > PD2 > AUX." (at 379.73 31.75 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid cc759bbd-2277-548e-9a9f-12adb8ac7179))

(text "NOTE: no wires used - connectivity is via matching label names (valid KiCad practice)." (at 20.32 219.71 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid 3dd54bdf-17a0-5b67-ab61-534daae95195))
(text "BMS J2: 1 raw negative, 2 cell2 tap, 3 raw positive, 4 cell1 tap. Verify the assembled harness before connecting cells." (at 20.32 226.06 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid 3886ff1c-0d63-59d7-b23c-57319cf2548a))
(text "U719 BQ7791500 autonomously protects each cell at 4.20V OV / 2.90V UV and drives back-to-back low-side FETs." (at 20.32 232.41 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid aeb86f5b-f4fd-536d-a253-a70a83d15436))
(text "RS11=8mOhm gives 7.5A nominal OCD and 15A nominal SCD; U11/RS10 and F1 remain independent tighter/secondary protection." (at 20.32 237.49 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid bd2cc33c-5cdf-5d1c-9876-9e0f3e5dc95e))
(text "Three insulated cell probes drive raw-referenced BMS comparators and CTRC/CTRD. U719 TS retains its unused-function strap." (at 20.32 243.84 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid 725b3ad7-1def-55e1-a2f7-3f0fffd021a5))

(text "ISL9241 starts with a 200mA input limit and charging off. Firmware must verify the source and program bounded limits." (at 20.32 256.54 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid 0668b772-ee3c-56d1-b434-ca023b1e1908))



(text "RS2600 is the 20mOhm input shunt. RS2601 is the separate 10mOhm battery-current shunt; both need Kelvin routing." (at 20.32 294.64 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid e13cf0f5-faed-5223-820f-0f985b03c437))

(text "U11 accepts about 8.45-13.57V nominal; 11mOhm RS10 gives 4.55A nominal and <=5.51A worst-case trips." (at 20.32 309.88 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid 5467c761-d281-571d-80ca-a176ab678e39))

(text "STARTUP: keep Mu enable low and PROCHOT asserted. Read TCPC PD Status 0x40 and active PDO/RDO 0x34/0x35 before selecting a source." (at 20.32 325.12 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid 875af184-1e23-5bee-8cdf-bbc916ee0215))
(text "Require the qualified VSYS threshold before Mu enable and confirm MU_12V_PG. Source, charger, watchdog or PG faults revoke enable; profile gates remain off until qualified." (at 20.32 332.74 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid 9cde9aea-189d-5bd1-814c-d4864f08389d))


(text "USB and VSYS use reverse-blocking ideal-diode feeds. AUX uses D711. The EC can start from 5V USB before the main source paths are enabled." (at 20.32 355.6 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid c7ff8252-fe55-5b05-b6cb-c1d057c8f39a))
(text "5V and 9V adapters use the buck-boost path. Running and charging share the measured input budget; a qualified pack can cover a shortfall." (at 20.32 363.22 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid de7d58df-42df-5fd2-96e1-9088282f20ed))
(text "C746 provides low-ESR hold-up through LTC4418 break-before-make source switching." (at 20.32 370.84 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid bdcdb364-24ae-5a80-ad81-ea04fe7aa243))
















